## 2026-03-16

Work Session: 4 hours

Objective

Identify the primary latency bottleneck within the Whisper inference pipeline for short banking voice commands.

---

Tasks Completed

* Updated profiling framework to use the MINDS-14 banking subset
* Implemented stage-level latency measurements in profiling/profile_whisper.py
* Measured execution time for:

  * audio loading
  * audio padding/trimming
  * mel spectrogram generation
  * encoder forward pass
  * decoder execution
* Executed profiling experiments on the banking command dataset
* Generated baseline profiling results

---

Configuration

* Dataset: MINDS-14 Banking Subset
* Number of Files: 41
* Audio Duration: ≤ 4 seconds
* Intents:

  * atm_limit
  * balance
  * card_issues
  * cash_deposit
  * latest_transactions
  * pay_bill
* Model: Whisper Small
* Device: CPU
* Decoding Method: whisper.decode()
* Language: English

---

Results Summary

Typical latency ranges observed:

* Audio Loading: ~90–140 ms
* Pad/Trim: ~1 ms
* Mel Spectrogram: ~4–12 ms
* Encoder: ~1300–1450 ms
* Decoder: ~1700–2100 ms
* Total Inference Time: ~3100–3600 ms

---

Key Observation

The decoder stage consistently required more processing time than any other component.

Approximate contribution:

* Decoder: 55–60%
* Encoder: 35–40%
* Preprocessing: <5%

---

Interpretation

The Whisper decoder is the primary latency bottleneck when processing short banking voice commands.

Although encoder execution contributes significantly to overall latency, decoder execution remains the dominant source of delay and represents the most promising optimization target.

---

Research Contribution

This experiment identified the principal latency bottleneck within the Whisper inference pipeline.

The findings provide a data-driven basis for focusing subsequent optimization efforts on decoder performance rather than preprocessing or feature extraction stages.

---

